1
00:07:56,000 --> 00:08:02,000
The West was never this far west.

2
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Quigley Down Under is a western film directed by Simon Wincer.

3
00:23:48,000 --> 00:23:54,000
American Matt Quigley answers Australian land baron Elliott Marston's ad
for a sharpshooter to kill the dingoes on his property.

4
00:31:44,000 --> 00:31:50,000
But when Quigley finds out that Marston's real target is
the aborigines, Quigley hits the road.

5
00:39:40,000 --> 00:39:46,000
Now, even American expatriate Crazy Cora can't keep Quigley safe in
his cat-and-mouse game with the homicidal Marston.

6
00:47:36,000 --> 00:47:42,000
Matthew Quigley, played by Tom Selleck.

7
00:55:32,000 --> 00:55:38,000
Crazy Cora, played by Laura San Giacomo.

8
01:03:28,000 --> 01:03:34,000
Elliott Marston, played by Alan Rickman.

9
01:11:24,000 --> 01:11:30,000
Major Ashley-Pitt, played by Chris Haywood.

10
01:19:20,000 --> 01:19:26,000
Grimmelman, played by Ron Haddrick.

11
01:27:16,000 --> 01:27:22,000
Dobkin, played by Tony Bonner.

12
01:35:12,000 --> 01:35:18,000
Quigley Down Under is a 1990 Western genre film, directed by Simon Wincer and starring
Tom Selleck, Alan Rickman, and Laura San Giacomo, and set in Australia.

13
01:43:08,000 --> 01:43:14,000
Although it opened to generally poor reviews, it has
since developed an enduring niche following.

14
01:51:04,000 --> 01:51:10,000
The film explores themes of chase, indigenous australians,
australian outback, fremantle, australian western.
